SEG = "LIC"
CAT = "fnswLicence"
Q = [
    ("Under s 18 of the Firearms Act, an NSW firearms licence must contain:",
     "Recent photo of the holder", ["Holder's GP's name", "Holder's tax number", "Photo of their gun safe at home"],
     "Section 18(2) requires a licence to carry a recent photograph and the signature of the licensee, the licence category, the registered firearms, the genuine reason and a reference to the storage requirements."),
    ("The 28-day waiting period before an NSW licence can be issued does not apply to:",
     "Licence renewal", ["A first category A licence", "A first category B licence", "Any primary producer"],
     "Section 11(2) says a licence must not be issued until 28 days after the application is made, but s 11(2A) exempts renewals, including a renewal that adds category A or B."),
    ("A new NSW firearms licence stays in force for up to:",
     "2 years", ["1 year", "5 years", "10 years"],
     "Section 21 says a licence continues in force for 2 years, or a shorter prescribed period, unless surrendered or revoked. The NSW Government confirmed that the 5-year term ended on 1 July 2026."),
    ("A licence that was issued with a 5-year term before 1 July 2026:",
     "Runs until it expires", ["Ended on 1 July 2026", "Was cut to two years", "Must be reissued at once"],
     "Clause 40 of Schedule 3 keeps the old s 21 for licences already in force, and the NSW Government said licences issued before 1 July 2026 remain valid until expiry."),
    ("Which of these is never a genuine reason for an NSW firearms licence?",
     "Personal protection", ["Primary production", "Animal welfare", "Firearms collection"],
     "Section 12(2) says the protection of yourself or any other person is not a genuine reason. Primary production, animal welfare and firearms collection are all listed in the Table to s 12."),
    ("A licence was issued for sport/target shooting only. May the holder use the rifle to hunt?",
     "No, only for target shooting", ["Yes, on any rural land", "Yes, with the club's written consent", "Yes, outside club days"],
     "A licence authorises use of a firearm only for the purpose established as the genuine reason. Using it for another purpose is an offence under s 7A(2), unless hunting is also a reason on the licence."),
    ("Apart from the land's owner or occupier, who can give permission to shoot on rural land for the recreational hunting reason?",
     "NPWS officer or employee", ["Any local council officer", "Neighbouring farmer", "Land's real estate agent"],
     "The Table to s 12 accepts permission from the owner or occupier of rural land, or from an officer or employee of the National Parks and Wildlife Service, the Department of Primary Industries and Regional Development or another prescribed authority."),
    ("Without land of their own or a landowner's permission, a person can still show recreational hunting as a reason by being:",
     "Approved hunting club member", ["Approved pistol club member", "Registered firearm owner", "A former Defence member"],
     "The Table to s 12 lists current membership of a hunting club approved by the Commissioner as one way to establish recreational hunting/vermin control."),
    ("Permission to shoot on land managed under the Forestry Act 2012 must come from:",
     "That land's manager", ["Nearest police station", "Any adjoining landowner", "Local council"],
     "Paragraph (b1) of the recreational hunting reason accepts proof of permission given by a land manager within the meaning of the Forestry Act 2012 for land they manage."),
    ("The genuine reason of primary production requires the applicant to state they will use the firearm solely:",
     "For farming or grazing", ["On weekends only", "For target practice", "Near the farm's homestead"],
     "The Table to s 12 says a primary producer must state they intend to use the firearm solely in connection with farming or grazing, including suppressing vertebrate pest animals on the land."),
    ("A veterinary practitioner who may need to destroy suffering animals can rely on the genuine reason of:",
     "Animal welfare", ["Primary production", "Sport/target shooting", "Vertebrate pest control"],
     "The animal welfare reason in the Table to s 12 lists appointed animal welfare officers of approved charities, veterinary practitioners, certain DPIRD and Local Land Services staff, and animal handlers who may need to destroy animals to avoid suffering."),
    ("For the genuine reason of firearms collection, the approved collectors' society must confirm the collection has:",
     "Genuine historical value", ["At least ten firearms in it", "Public display licence", "Its own insurance cover"],
     "The Table to s 12 requires a written statement from an approved collectors' society or club that the collection has a genuine commemorative, historical, thematic or financial value."),
    ("If an applicant does not give the identity verification consents and documents in the time required, the application is:",
     "Taken to be withdrawn", ["Approved after 28 days", "Sent to a magistrate", "Delayed for a year"],
     "Section 10(2A) says the application is taken to have been withdrawn. Since 1 July 2026 identity verification is mandatory before a licence or permit application can proceed."),
    ("Before a licence is issued, the Commissioner must be satisfied the applicant is a resident of:",
     "NSW, or soon to be", ["Australia, for 5 years", "Any Australian state", "The same council area"],
     "Section 11(3)(d) requires the Commissioner to be satisfied the applicant is a resident of New South Wales or is about to become one."),
    ("Before a first NSW firearms licence is issued, a person who has never held one must have completed:",
     "Approved safety course", ["Year of club shooting", "Full hunting season", "Senior first aid course"],
     "Section 11(3)(b) requires a person who has never held a licence to complete the firearms training and safety courses prescribed for that licence, to the Commissioner's satisfaction."),
    ("A licence must not be issued to a person who, within the previous 10 years, was subject to:",
     "Apprehended violence order", ["Noise abatement order", "Licence suspension for speeding", "Tenancy tribunal order"],
     "Section 11(5)(c) bars a person who is subject to an AVO or interim AVO, or was subject to an AVO (other than a revoked one) within 10 years before applying."),
    ("A licence must not be issued if there is reasonable cause to believe the applicant may not keep responsible control of firearms because of:",
     "Previous suicide attempt", ["Recent change of job", "Being self-employed", "A first-time application"],
     "Section 11(4) lists the applicant's way of living or domestic circumstances, any previous attempt at suicide or self-inflicted injury, and intemperate habits or unsound mind."),
    ("A firearms licence is automatically suspended when the licensee:",
     "Has an interim AVO made", ["Changes their address", "Buys a second firearm", "Misses a club shoot"],
     "Section 23 suspends a licence automatically on the making of an interim apprehended violence order, until the order is confirmed or revoked."),
    ("If a licence is suspended or revoked, the holder must surrender their firearms and licence to a police officer:",
     "Immediately", ["Within 7 days", "Within 28 days", "At the next renewal"],
     "Section 25(1) requires the person to surrender any firearm in their possession, and the licence, to a police officer immediately."),
    ("A licence is automatically revoked when the licensee becomes subject to:",
     "Firearms prohibition order", ["Interim AVO being made", "Formal police caution", "Club membership suspension"],
     "Section 24(1) revokes a licence automatically on a firearms prohibition order, an apprehended violence order or a serious domestic abuse prevention order. An interim AVO suspends rather than revokes."),
    ("The Commissioner may revoke a licence if, through the licensee's negligence:",
     "A firearm was lost or stolen", ["Their club lost members", "Their range closed early", "A renewal letter was late"],
     "Section 24(2)(c1) allows revocation if the licensee, through negligence or fraud, caused a firearm to be lost or stolen."),
    ("If the Commissioner is aware a licensee has been charged with a domestic violence offence, the Commissioner must:",
     "Suspend the licence", ["Wait for the trial result", "Book a storage inspection", "Send a warning letter"],
     "Section 22(2) requires the Commissioner to suspend the licence when aware of a domestic violence charge, or with reasonable cause to believe one was committed or threatened."),
    ("While a licence is suspended, it authorises the holder to possess or use firearms:",
     "Not at all", ["Only at home", "Only at an approved range", "Only for pest control"],
     "Section 22(3) says a suspended licence does not authorise the possession or use of firearms during the period in the suspension notice."),
    ("An interstate category A licence holder notifies the Commissioner of a permanent move to NSW. Their licence counts as an NSW licence for up to:",
     "3 months", ["7 days", "28 days", "12 months"],
     "Under s 27(2), an interstate category A or B licence is taken to be the corresponding NSW licence for 3 months from notification, or until the NSW application is decided, whichever is sooner."),
    ("An interstate category H licence holder notifies the Commissioner of a move to NSW. Their licence counts in NSW for:",
     "7 days", ["3 months", "28 days", "2 years"],
     "Under s 27(3), an interstate category C, D or H licence counts for 7 days. Someone who applies within that time is not committing an offence while the application is decided."),
    ("A resident of another state holding an equivalent category A licence may use a category A firearm in NSW without an NSW licence when:",
     "Competing in an approved shoot", ["Hunting on any NSW rural land", "Visiting friends or family in NSW", "Driving across NSW"],
     "Section 26(1) exempts interstate holders of an equivalent A, B or H licence only to take part in a shooting competition approved by the Commissioner, or another prescribed purpose."),
    ("The first underlying principle of the Firearms Act says possessing and using a firearm is:",
     "Conditional privilege", ["Right of every adult", "Right of rural residents", "Privilege of club members"],
     "Section 3(1)(a) confirms firearm possession and use as a privilege conditional on the overriding need to ensure public safety."),
    ("Except for dealers and the business or employment reason, an NSW firearms licence can be issued only to:",
     "Natural person", ["Registered company", "Shooting club", "Family trust"],
     "Section 11(6) says that, apart from a firearms dealer licence or a business or employment reason, a licence must not be issued to a person who is not a natural person."),
]
